 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Petrol is **13.5% more expensive** than a year ago. In August 2026, the latest month published, the ABS automotive fuel index was 112.95, against 99.49 in August 2025.\n\nIn dollar terms, a $80 tank in August 2025 would cost about $91 now, so roughly $11 more per fill. I can't see actual pump prices, so this is based on the CPI fuel index, not your local servo.\n\nThe increase has been uneven over the past year:\n- **Early 2025:** fuel was falling, down 5–12% year on year from February to July.\n- **March–May 2026:** a sharp spike, up 24.2% in March and 18.6% in April compared with a year earlier.\n- **June 2026:** prices dropped back, down 7.3% year on year.\n- **August 2026:** prices climbed again, up 13.5%.",
